september 1944  southeast of japan uss finback steams  toward the crash site of an american  plane  10 miles away a young pilot drifts  towards the shores of a japanese island  from which enemy ships set out towards  him  the situation appears hopeless  until two american planes from his  squadron appear overhead  the avenger aircraft strafe the japanese  vessels  and they retreat to the protection of  the shore  but now low on fuel the american planes  must return to their carrier  the aviator is vulnerable and alone  again  to the south uss finn back approaches  the coordinates of the downed airmen  guided in by its air cover  at last a lookout spots a bright yellow  object in the vast pacific  [Music]  from the life raft after more than three  hours of fear and struggle  the twenty-year-old pilot believes he  has started to hallucinate  as he sees what he describes as an  apparition  first a dark spot  then a submarine emerges  he worries it might be japanese  but he identifies the men on board with  relief  they are american  uss finback's photographic officer rolls  his camera  five submariners gather at finback's bow  to recover the bobbing life raft  [Music]  just before noon more than three hours  after the crash  they pulled the young pilot aboard  [Music]  he is safe  [Music]  you
 

